WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.730
This girl is Kouyama Mitsuki. 12 years old!

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.310
The recording day for her debut song, "Myself", had come...

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.680
And then that Takuto...

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.110
He fell asleep while he was a stuffed animal, and some strange girl picked him up.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.610
That's because he's such an oaf.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.960
Mitsuki managed to get him back, though.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.490
Her recording went off without a hitch.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.280
Takuto.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.990
I'll keep this a secret from the chief, 'kay?

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.070
Well, then...

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.870
...I wonder what's going to happen today.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:23.450
Huh?{missing line}

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.620
Do you understand?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.730
Yes.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.510
Well then.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.090
We still have another song for you!

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.260
In just a moment... we'll have the song that all eyes are on this week.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:10.140
Isn't it amazing? Here it is...

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.710
...on sale this week... the song, "Myself".

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.720
This song is actually...

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.810
...from the artist who made Seed Records' New Artist audition...

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.690
...in just one try... the debut song for <i>Full Moon...</i>

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.770
...is produced by Takasu Kohei.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:24.780
However, Takasu-san was unable to join us for an interview during this break.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.970
Um... excuse me.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.240
Can you please turn off the radio?

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.860
Which brings us to the song that's caught everyone's attention!

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.200
I detest music.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:28.200
Listen to this.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.120
Ah. Yes.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.160
<i>Full Moon's...</i>

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.210
Welcome back, madam.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.480
Where's Mitsuki-san?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.660
Ah. She's resting in her room.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.610
Is that so?

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.540
Has she done anything peculiar?

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:50.720
Oh man!

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.470
This manga is a riot!

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.520
What is that vulgar behavior, Mitsuki-san?

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:57.060
Geh!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.310
Please excuse me, Grandmother.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.490
I'll be more careful next time!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.410
Geez...

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.330
She's only twelve, for crying out loud. {LOL Meroko said 10, correction edit XD}

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:18.960
Ah...

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.920
Those guys... they're so lucky... {Again with the Takuto-tachi, drives me bonkers}

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.840
They're probably in Shibuya right now, huh?

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.470
Wow...

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.750
What are you staring at?

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.330
This is your first live concert, isn't it?

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.690
Where are you performing?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.750
Where, indeed...

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.480
Ah?

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.120
You're so helpless.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.610
I'll go look for it.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.570
Where did your manager say it was...?

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.800
That...she didn't tell me.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.010
"I'll know when I reach the center."

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.430
Hey, where exactly is this "center"?

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:55.950
Hmm...

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.120
Over there.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.340
Wow!

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.170
Wow!

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.410
Man, you're such a hick? {Hick: Unsophisticated, simpleton, country bumpkin = Pointless, Stupid Note, not as bad as keikaku though}

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.110
That's because this is my first time in Shibuya!

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:13.390
Wow...

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.560
Anyways, where exactly are we?

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:17.520
Oh?

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.520
Why are they all looking up?

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:21.130
Eh?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:30.950
Wow!

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:31.740
Who is that?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.430
It's that girl.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.030
You know, the one who was 
chosen at that audition.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:34.570
{BAD FRAME}

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.300
I know her.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.110
I heard her song on the radio.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.750
Ah... that girl, huh?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.540
She's really cute.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.950
They said you're cute.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.110
How does the <i>object of worship</i>  feel about it?

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.380
Hmm?

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:49.670
What's wrong?

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.670
Why...?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.180
For some reason... that doesn't look like me...

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.010
You could say...

00:04:57.010 --> 00:04:59.790
...that there's a gap between what's real and what's just an image.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:01.140
Really...

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.110
Please line up over here!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.150
Wow!

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.000
Today is Full Moon's special live concert.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.600
Those who wish to enjoy it...

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.190
...please line up over here.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.370
There's this many people gathered for a new artist who hasn't even debuted, huh?

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.370
In-Incredible.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.830
I'm going to sing in front of this many people... {merged lines for better phrasing}

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.690
What's wrong?

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.020
C-Can I sing well, I wonder?

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.030
What if I get the words wrong..?{question mark}

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.320
When that happens...

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:35.610
<i>"When that happens..."</i>{italic and quotation}

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.010
Smile and make it up! {Protip}

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:38.470
I don't want to do that!

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.810
I worked so hard to come up with those lyrics.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.100
So you won't get them wrong, right?

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.540
Like I said...

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.940
I'm worried I can do it.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:47.730
Hey, hey.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.070
Now is not the time to 
start thinking like that.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:51.560
Anyways...

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.990
We have to find somewhere to transform you.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:54.240
Over there.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:26.690
Let's see... The exit is...

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.190
You're <i>Full Moon,</i> aren't you?

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.990
Don't you remember me? {Mitsuki doesn't remember sore losers}

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:34.570
Eh?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.950
Have we met somewhere before?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.910
At the beginning of the audition.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.120
Um...

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.170
Um...

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.990
You don't remember?

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.270
Ah... sorry. {but I don't remember losers}

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.300
I... was the one after you. {LOL, YOU HAD NO SHOT BECAUSE MITSUKI PWNED EVERYONE}

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.050
Eh?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.140
I was Number 22 at the audition.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.780
Thanks to you...

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.350
I had to go home without auditioning. {Oh boo-hoo *plays the world's smallest violin}

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.400
I'm very sorry.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.240
Oh.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.000
It's not something you need to apologize for.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.370
Eh...

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.680
That's right.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.450
If someone gets chosen...

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.680
...everyone else is disappointed.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:27.080
That's right.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.240
Because I...

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.790
...don't think that I would have lost to you. {GET THE F OUTTA HERE XD}

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:31.250
Eh?

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.450
If I had gone instead of you...

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:35.710
I would have been the one chosen instead. {Coulda, woulda, shoulda}

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:37.090
That...

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.680
I suppose that could have happened...

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:39.840
Because...

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.800
I'm an incredible singer. {Translation: I'm a talentless hack}

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.660
A-Ah...

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.000
Good to see she doesn't lack self-confidence.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:46.980
It's so beneficial...

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.100
...that cuteness of yours.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:48.480
Eh?

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.060
What do you mean?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:51.020
Oh?

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.060
You didn't know?

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.360
You weren't chosen for you singing...

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.280
The decision was based solely on your looks. {Shani: Then they did great! Mitsuki is so damn cute!}

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:56.950
Eh?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.040
If it wasn't for that, there's no way you would have been selected...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.720
...with such a mediocre song.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:04.860
Today's concert...

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:06.280
I'm looking forward to it.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.670
You can do all sorts of tricks with the mic for your CD, but...

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.200
...you can't do something
 like that for a live concert.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.580
With only your looks...

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.670
Having to sing in front of flocks of people...

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.590
It'd be best if you realized your position as soon as possible.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.990
That's such a spiteful girl. {What a spiteful *will end it there}

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:26.640
Hmm?

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:39.360
Isn't she late?

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:40.560
That's right...

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.570
Maybe she got the place wrong...

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:44.580
Yes?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.490
She's arrived.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:47.700
Ah. She's here! She's here!

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.900
Sorry for being late.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:49.750
Look! Look!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.490
Isn't that a great poster?

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.330
I saw it.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.340
It's the first time you've seen yourself like that, isn't it? {a.f.k forgot it after isn't, fixed}

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:57.990
It was Takasu-san's idea 
to go all-out and be flashy.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:58.690
Well?

00:08:58.690 --> 00:08:59.650
Were you surprised?

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:00.340
Ah.

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:01.460
I was.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.100
Hmm?

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.390
Are you nervous?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:06.390
N-No...

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:09.310
I've been through this before, too...

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.280
When you were an idol, right?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.440
That's right. {Bad memories written on her face}

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.560
The first stage I debuted on...

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.600
...was at a poolside in an amusement park, though.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.740
Right in font of the stage, I was frozen stiff with nervousness.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.730
After the other idols saw that, they taught me...

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.990
..at times like this...

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.580
...in the palm of your hand...

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.540
Write <i>hitto.</i> {Can't realy do anything with this one}

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.160
Then, you take a deep breath.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.250
If you do that, you won't get nervous.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:37.360
Eh?

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.090
That's wrong, Ooshige-chan.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.000
Not <i>hitto</i>, it's <i>hito.</i>

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.170
Hito as in humans.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.470
Eh?! Really?!

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:47.350
Then... then... I didn't make it because of that?!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.800
Ah! I was tricked! Damn it!

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.390
Give me back my youth!

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:52.140
Give it back!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:52.730
Give it back!!

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:57.060
Give it back!!!

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:00.320
Mitsuki, be sure to write <i>hito</i>  properly.

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:01.400
O-Okay.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:02.990
Ah...

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.320
Um... Ooshige-san.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:05.110
Ah?

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:05.680
Hmm?

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.470
Was I chosen at the audition...

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.080
...because I look cute?

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.790
Who told you that?

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.500
Um...

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:18.750
Who...? Well...

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.590
My ears seem to be failing me.

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.140
Can you say that again?

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.740
It doesn't matter how well I sing...?

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:32.600
Of course it matters.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.450
I don't know who told you this, but...

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.440
...you made the audition, and today's...

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.500
Um... you should get ready soon...

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.000
It's almost time.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:41.740
That's right.

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:43.550
It's all in your hands now, then.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:44.070
Okay!

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:45.780
Anyways...

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:48.130
Just focus on the live concert right now.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.030
Ah... s-sure.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.550
Come over here, then. {this is one of the make-up ladies calling Mitsuki}

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.160
Oh... me too.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.400
Wow! It's crazy outside!

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.560
There are lines all the way down the street.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.270
I'll have to do a perfect job here.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:05.320
Can I come in?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:06.400
Yes!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:08.650
Huh?

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:09.360
Where is she?

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.660
The bathroom.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:11.530
I see.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:12.840
Takasu-san.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:13.880
Do you want to eat this?

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.890
It's a new potato product.

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:17.080
Hmm. It looks good.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:54.780
So you were up here, huh?

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.250
Takuto...

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.360
Takuto... I...

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.000
Ah?

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:07.170
No!

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.090
W-What are you doing?!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:11.680
Ah!

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.180
My hair's all messed up!

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:14.680
You're so mean!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.800
And they just made me look pretty...!

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:17.170
Hmph!

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.220
A singer who only depends on looks...

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:21.270
Of course you're concerned about your appearance, right?

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:21.640
Ah...

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.200
Have I said too much?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.770
Should I beg for forgiveness, too?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.030
The birth of the industry's first idol in disguise...

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.400
...you've become the topic of 
discussion everywhere.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.150
Hmph!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.320
Where are you going?

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.240
Are you running away?

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:36.060
Sing like you're supposed to.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.160
I'm going to sing.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:39.160
Because that's my job.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:40.960
Ah?

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:42.710
What?!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:43.080
Eh?

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:43.670
W-What?

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.680
Who do you think you are, 
saying it's just a job!

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.280
No matter how hard it gets...

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.820
...you're going to smile and do your best, because it's your job?!

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.720
I didn't say anything like that!

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:54.240
<i>"Because it's my job..."</i>{Quotation}

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.170
If you're going to have such 
a cold attitude about it...

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.260
...you won't be able to 
touch anyone's heart.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:58.720
Eh?

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.980
You need to enjoy singing 
from the heart first.

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:03.770
Ah.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:06.860
I see...

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:08.440
That's right...

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:09.650
But...

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.070
Right now, I...

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.220
I haven't mentioned it before, but...

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.370
When you auditioned...

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.290
Back then, I...

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.870
...was surprised and moved.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:22.500
Eh?

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:25.540
You sang with such a beautiful voice.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:28.500
Somehow, it didn't seem like a voice...

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.210
...more like an aura of sound.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.050
Even the lower tones came through clearly.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.970
It was like a dream.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:39.180
That such a singer existed...

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:40.470
...I was overjoyed.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:43.620
Back then...

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:45.210
...I was happy, too!

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:49.400
It's been so long since 
I'd sung in such a loud voice...

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:51.570
Breathing didn't hurt either.

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:54.260
It may seem normal to most people, but...

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.660
...to be able to use that kind of voice...

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.400
...makes me very happy!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.830
Singing... is all about expressing 
your feelings, isn't it?

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.710
If I sing without confidence...

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.750
...that's what the people 
who are listening will hear.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:10.500
Ah...

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.960
But, still... I...

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:14.440
It's fine. It's fine.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:15.510
Don't worry about it.

00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:16.300
Huh?

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:17.930
Yep!

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:22.810
Okay! I'm going!

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:30.270
Ah!

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:31.940
Ah. Ooshige-san.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:32.570
Mitsuki.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.780
Over there. Look at that!

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:34.240
Eh?

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:41.700
Eh?

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.960
What is this?

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.450
A huge mountain of postcards...

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.620
These are all advance orders sent to this store for your CD.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:48.080
Eh?

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.200
It seems like a lot, but...

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.920
...these are just the orders from this store.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.890
Full Moon's Debut Single...

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.220
I am placing an advanced order for "Myself".

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:04.140
<i>Please fulfill my request.</i>

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:06.230
<i>I heard it on the radio...</i>

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.020
<i>and loved it after just one listen.</i>

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.630
<i>It's a really great song, isn't it?</i>

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:13.080
<i>It's the best!</i>

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.500
<i>I wonder what the girl who sang it is like.</i>

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:19.060
<i>I'm very interested.</i>

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:20.950
<i>She's a young girl, but...</i>

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.390
<i>...she has a pleasing voice.</i>

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.760
<i>It cleanses the soul.</i>

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:29.540
This was the response to your publicity single that's airing on the radio.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:29.960
Ah?

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.090
You weren't just "chosen for your looks."

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.320
You believe me, right?

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:58.940
Takasu-san! {exclamatory added}

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.940
What a trick you've set up!

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:02.900
That was an amazing display.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:05.400
Ooshige-chan sure knows what she's doing...

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:42.980
It was wonderful, Takasu-san!

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:44.900
It was really wonderful, Ooshige-chan!{timing fix: start}

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.450
I just felt that I should do something for her.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:00.210
Ah.

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:01.090
You're...

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.210
I've lost.

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:04.760
Eh?

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.640
I'm no match for you.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:09.440
Your singing was too good.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.010
It only makes sense that you were chosen.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:14.700
Which is why...

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.140
...for saying all that...

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:17.480
...I'm ashamed of myself.

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.180
I'm really sorry. {Bow to the master}

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:22.480
It's okay.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.460
I have faith in my singing, but...

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:28.230
...I'm going to work even harder!

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:29.940
Me, too...

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.980
In order to share my 
feelings with everyone...

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.100
...I have to work hard!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.500
We have to both work hard, right?

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:37.610
You're right.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:51.160
You really were here.

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:52.300
Thanks for earlier.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.360
It wasn't much... just some 
feathers floating around.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.140
Not that...

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:56.560
Eh?

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:59.290
What you told me earlier...

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:01.480
You were trying to cheer me up, right?

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.360
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:06.860
I just can't stand people who 
hesitate and constantly worry.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:08.570
Hey!

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:09.740
Are you listening to me?!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.120
In the end... you got them across...

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.580
...your feelings, right?{replaced "yeah" with "right"}

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:06.980
That girl's song...

00:23:06.980 --> 00:23:08.020
It's a huge hit!

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:09.400
The kids at school are probably...

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:11.440
...all talking about <i>Full Moon.</i>

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:12.740
Of course!

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:15.030
Even the manager said it was a great hit.

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:15.780
Huh?

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:17.870
Nobody's talking about <i>Full Moon,</i> huh?

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:18.580
All right!

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:19.870
If nobody's heard of her...

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:21.290
...I'll let them all know!

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:22.740
Leave it to me!

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:23.980
Wait, Meroko!

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:27.080
If you go out, you'll let something slip again!

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:29.500
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:31.210
Is It Really a Hit?
